2026-08-15 14:37:01,782 1093478 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'goal', 'text': 'The progress that actually happened is visible from the page Peter lands on.\n\nRaised by device after looking at the board in a browser; verified here rather than taken on report. They searched the rendered overview for *matches*, *unclear* and *verif* and got nothing.\n\nFive aggregate places a number could go — top bar, overview AREAS table, area Stats tab — and the **matches** axis is in none of them. It exists only on a per-area Specs tab, one area at a time.\n\n**The board is showing the axis that cannot move.** Measured, 0.31s across the corpus: `matches 159 · never 192 · contradicts 6 · unclear 13`, against `works 32 of 370`. `works` cannot move until the firmware builds. `matches` went 0 → 159 today. So the landing page says *32 of 370* and has said so all day, while the thing that moved needs seven area pages and a tab in each.\n\n**That is the founding complaint, reproduced by the tool built to answer it.** Peter stopped coding because he could not see progress.\n\nDone means: both axes adjacent and unmerged in aggregate, `contradicts` visible from the landing page, each project showing its own figures, both themes.'}
2026-08-15 14:37:12,818 1093478 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'plan', 'text': 'Spec: `docs/modules/showing-progress.md`, attached.\n\n**Files:** `db.py` (`match_totals`), `app.py` (`_vitals`, `_rows`, the overview), `render.py` (the evidence strip, the AREAS table).\n\n**The rule that governs every choice here** is device\'s, and it is the reason the split exists: *whatever you add must not merge into a single number.* Two numbers, always adjacent, never summed. The most informative thing on the page is that one axis is racing and the other is stuck.\n\n- **Evidence gains a second row.** It is the signature element and duplicating the grid puts the two rates at the same scale — nothing explains "one moved, one did not" faster than two identical grids with visibly different fill.\n- **Top bar gains `matches` beside `proven`**, so they read as a pair.\n- **`contradicts` gets its own cell only when non-zero**, styled bad. A permanent cell showing zero stops being read.\n- **AREAS table gains a `matches` column** next to `proven`.\n\n**Not doing:** no combined percentage, no single bar, no change to what `proven` means, and `never` is not shown — it is the complement and printing it invites the reader to do arithmetic the page should have done.\n\n**Cost is measured, not assumed:** `verify_state` across all 370 claims is 0.31s, so no batching. Re-measure after, because this now runs on the landing page of every project.'}
