2026-08-15 16:47:13,630 1093478 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'goal', 'text': 'One database with a project column, so a question can span projects.\n\n**Peter overruled the separate-database design on 2026-08-15:** *"not sure I agree with 1 db per project"*, then *"so that\'s what is needed one database."*\n\n**Raised, ruled and scheduled through specboard itself** — his answer to *"as this is dogfood how is that going to be managed / controlled?"* The defect is `the-pages/a-database-per-project-hides-the-cross-project-question`, `accepted` by peter, work cut to this task. Getting that far required building `POST /defects/schedule`, because the board had been printing *"cut work from N defects"* with nothing behind it.\n\n**My justification for the original design was wrong, and specifically in its number.** I wrote "a project column across 23 tables" in the spec, a code comment and a commit message. Counted properly: **8 tables reach `area` by foreign key and inherit project for free**, 5 more carry a bare `area` column, and only ~10 top-level tables genuinely need it — `area`, `meta`, `rc`, `resource`, `request`, `queue`, `run`, `resource_check`, `request_event`, `proof_needs`.\n\n**What separate databases make impossible, which is the real argument:**\n- *"What is waiting on me across everything"* — Peter has one attention, not one per project.\n- `build-the-queue` cannot be built at all: "what is next" has no scope to be next within.\n- `sqlite3 board.db` stops answering anything global, which quietly falsified this repo\'s own RESOURCES row.\n\nThe isolation benefit I claimed was largely theoretical, and the `--import` guard now covers the blast radius that motivated it.\n\n**`area` must become keyed `(project, name)` regardless** — nothing today stops two projects both having a `camera`.\n\nDone means: one database, both projects intact with their real content, round-trip lossless for both, and a cross-project question answered by a query.'}
