2026-08-15 17:28:26,097 1093478 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_notes_set args={'number': 1, 'text': '**DECIDED BY PETER, 2026-08-15. Requests and the queue are PROJECT-SCOPED.**\n\nHis words: *"I dont think so, it belongs to a project"* and *"if I ask a question in one project and then switch projects, how would that question be relevant to another project"*.\n\nHe is right and I had argued the opposite. My reasoning was that he has one attention, so a request that disappears when he switches project is lost from view. That conflated two different things: being **able** to ask a cross-project question when you want one, and **mixing** every project\'s requests into every project\'s page. A request against `device` has no meaning on `specboard`\'s page — showing it there is noise, not safety.\n\nOne database still gives the first without doing the second: an "everything waiting on me" view becomes possible as a deliberate view, rather than every page becoming that view by accident.\n\n**So the schema:** `project` on `request`, `request_event` and `queue`, exactly as on `area`, `resource`, `rc` and `meta`. Nothing is board-global. If a cross-project view is ever wanted it is a query with no `project` predicate, which is precisely what one database buys and what separate databases made impossible.\n\nRecorded rather than left as an open DECIDE — Peter spotted that this step was still showing as pending after he had already answered it, which is the stale-mark failure this whole project exists to remove.'}
