2026-08-15 19:33:50,883 1158257 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'goal', 'text': 'Make a defect record correctable without losing what it said. The board could file a permanent record and could not correct one: `raising` and `ruling` both let a wrong entry be superseded, while `does`, `effect`, `where_` and `confidence` were written once by add_defect() and never again. That stopped being theoretical when the-store/who-is-taken-on-trust was filed through a double-quoted curl, the shell executed the backticks around `who`, and the output of the who command went into the corpus inside the defect about attribution — through seven passing checks, a LOSSLESS round trip and a commit. Done when a correction is an append-only event with a required reason and an unattributed-by-default author, the superseded text survives it, the corpus stops carrying the leaked output, and a check that starts its own throwaway board proves all of that over HTTP.'}
