2026-08-15 19:37:07,670 1158257 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'goal', 'text': 'Let a project be subscribed without shell access to the board\'s directory. Today the only way in is a human editing projects.yaml on this host and restarting, so a session in a new repo cannot begin the relationship at all. Peter\'s words: "subscription is a must, preferably by adding it via the dashboard or initiated by the agent" — the capability is mandatory, the two routes are preferred and not both mandated (device retracted the "both paths" paraphrase themselves). One POST /subscribe serves both callers, because an agent in another repo on this host can reach the board over HTTP; /xsession is the announcement convention, not a second mechanism. Done when a repo carrying only AREAS.yaml can subscribe over HTTP, is served WITHOUT a restart, and its overview does not open with a false UNEXPORTED alarm.'}
