2026-08-15 19:37:18,458 1158257 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'plan', 'text': "One `POST /subscribe` at board level, not under /p/<project>/, serving both callers: a form on the board for Peter and the same POST made directly by an agent in the new repo. Preconditions checked in order — repo given, path is a directory, docs/specs/AREAS.yaml exists, name not already registered — each refused with its own status and never a redirect. On success: append textually to projects.yaml (it carries comments a yaml.safe_dump would delete), create board-<name>.db, import, 303 to /p/<name>/. PROJECTS is re-read when projects.yaml's mtime changes, so a new project is reachable without a restart without putting a YAML parse on every page load. export.drift() stops counting a missing file as drift when the generated file would have no entries — asked of the database, not sniffed from the header — which is the day-one UNEXPORTED alarm. tools/check_subscribe.py over HTTP against a board it starts on a throwaway registry. Spec: docs/modules/subscribing-a-project.md"}
