2026-08-15 19:48:12,071 1158257 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'plan', 'text': 'DECIDED (Peter, 2026-08-15: "I dont think so, it belongs to a project"): requests and the queue are PROJECT-SCOPED. So `project` goes on the ~10 top-level tables — area, meta, rc, resource, request, request_event, queue, run, resource_check, proof_needs — and the other 13 inherit through `area`, which becomes keyed (project, name). Merge the two live databases with a one-off script that stamps every row with its source project; keep board.db as the surviving file so device\'s 370 claims never move. projects.yaml keeps its per-project `db:` key as a MIGRATION INPUT only. The round trip must still be lossless for BOTH projects afterwards or it is the provenance-block failure again, and a cross-project query must answer something neither database could. Spec: docs/modules/one-database.md'}
