2026-08-15 21:21:36,482 1180635 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'goal', 'text': 'Commits c08610e and 343f2ff shipped the LTC4150 input-offset correction (ioff) with no task and no spec. 343f2ff\'s own commit message cites "SPEC-IOFFSET" and the code references that name in six places (battery.h:456, main.cpp:339, api_help.h:57/134) — but docs/SPEC-IOFFSET.md does not exist. Write it, and fix the one live defect it exposes: floor_ma publishes a datasheet-derived guess (1.9 mA) when a measured value for the same quantity (ioff 2.3111 mA) is sitting in NVS.'}
2026-08-15 21:21:43,250 1180635 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'plan', 'text': 'Facts established by measurement this session, not recalled:\n\n- floor_ma is computed at src/main.cpp:423 as 0.0001/rsense*1000, i.e. an ASSUMED 100 uV VOS over the derived shunt. rsense itself is derived from quanta (main.cpp:899: 0.05 * 0.17067759/quanta). At quanta 0.16030799 that is 0.053234 ohm, giving floor_ma 1.8785 -> published as 1.9. Mechanism confirmed by arithmetic against the live device.\n- ioff is the MEASURED equivalent: 2.3111 mA, which across the same 0.053234 ohm is 123 uV — inside the datasheet VOS band but 23% above the assumed 100 uV.\n- floor_ma is not display-only: src/main.cpp:426 uses it as the below_floor predicate. Changing its source changes that flag\'s meaning, so the spec must state the intended semantics before the edit.\n- api_help.h:57 states the offset is "119 uV across the shunt". At the current quanta the arithmetic gives 123 uV. The help text is stale by a hair; check whether it is worth correcting or whether the quanta moved after it was written.\n\nOrder: spec first and shown to Peter for review BEFORE any source edit. No device writes and no reflash without his explicit go-ahead — the board is on c08610e-dirty and that is his call, not a side effect of this task.'}
