2026-08-16 07:36:10,836 1180635 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_new args={'name': 'ltc-mydash-silent-minify', 'title': "Make mydash's html2header.py fail loudly when terser exits non-zero, instead of silently corrupting the dashboard", 'steps': ['Edit minify_js: treat a non-zero terser exit as a failure and print why', 'Rebuild: confirm terser still runs (JS ratio ~31%)', 'Prove the fix is REACHED: hide terser from PATH, confirm it now warns, restore']}
2026-08-16 07:36:20,236 1180635 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'goal', 'text': 'SCOPE EXCEPTION, granted explicitly by Peter 2026-08-16: this edits /usr/share/pac/dev/pio/mylibs/mydash/scripts/html2header.py, OUTSIDE this repo\'s boundary. Normally a finding in another repo is raised via /xsession and never worked around — but Peter states no session owns mylibs, so there is no recipient to raise it to, and he ordered the fix directly.\n\nThe defect, verified by reading the source (not inherited from the handover): minify_js() wraps subprocess.run(["terser",...]) in try/except catching only FileNotFoundError and TimeoutExpired. A NON-ZERO EXIT is not an exception — it fails the `returncode == 0` test, falls past the return, and lands in the regex fallback. Nothing is printed on any of the three failure paths, while load_source() a few lines above does print on its failure path.\n\nThe fallback then runs re.sub(r\'//[^\\n]*\', \'\', js), which strips from // to end of line and therefore destroys any http:// inside a string literal. Net effect: a JS syntax error shipped into PROGMEM, a dashboard that will not parse, and the only visible signal is a ratio in a build line nobody reads (~15% instead of ~31%). This cost the previous session ~1 hour and it misdiagnosed the cause three times.\n\nTrigger in practice: /usr/local/bin/node v22 shadows Debian\'s v20 and does not search /usr/share/nodejs, so terser cannot resolve `commander` and exits non-zero.'}
2026-08-16 07:38:04,582 1180635 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_done args={'number': 1}
2026-08-16 07:38:15,121 1180635 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'plan', 'text': 'Fix applied to minify_js() in /usr/share/pac/dev/pio/mylibs/mydash/scripts/html2header.py: capture a reason on all four outcomes (non-zero exit with stderr, zero exit but empty output, terser missing, terser timeout) and print a two-line warning naming the exact corruption before falling through to the regex stripper. The fallback itself is unchanged — it still runs, so no build breaks; it just can no longer run silently.\n\nVERIFIED REACHED, both directions:\n- terser present  -> normal build, JS 49801->34120 (31.5%), no warning, SUCCESS in 40.6 s\n- fake terser exiting 1 with "Cannot find module \'commander\'" (the exact node-22 failure) -> warns with that stderr, RESULT: var u = "http:   <- corruption demonstrated\n- terser absent   -> warns "terser not on PATH", same corruption\n\nINCIDENTAL FINDING, not fixed: TWO tersers are installed.\n  /usr/bin/terser       -> ../share/nodejs/terser/bin/terser   (Debian, Feb 6 2025)\n  /usr/local/bin/terser -> ../lib/node_modules/terser/bin/terser (npm -g, Aug 15 18:47, previous session)\nDebian\'s already existed, so the npm install was probably unnecessary — the actual fault was node 22 shadowing node 20 and not searching /usr/share/nodejs. Two divergent copies now exist and whichever is first on PATH wins. Peter\'s call whether to remove the npm one.\n\nmylibs IS a git repo (toplevel /usr/share/pac/dev/pio/mylibs) and now shows ` M mydash/scripts/html2header.py`. NOT committed — committing in a repo this project does not own needs Peter\'s explicit go-ahead.'}
