2026-08-16 07:45:11,818 1180635 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'note', 'text': 'CORRECTION to the plan note above — I was WRONG that the npm terser was "probably unnecessary". Removing it broke the build immediately: Debian\'s /usr/bin/terser cannot run under Node 22 at all (Cannot find module \'commander\', because node 22 does not search /usr/share/nodejs). The npm copy was the ONLY working terser. My reasoning was that Debian\'s predated the npm one, so the npm one must be redundant — age is not evidence of function, and I did not run it before calling it redundant.\n\nCaught within one build by the warning added in step 1: JS 49801->41064 (17.6%) instead of 34120 (31.5%). The fix paid for itself inside ten minutes. It also left include/dashboard_html.h corrupt in the repo until rebuilt — that is the exact failure the warning exists to make visible, and it was visible.\n\nAlso correcting the session record: node is LIVE at v22.23.2. Peter said a previous session upgraded to 22 and reverted; the revert is not in effect now, and node 22 is the root cause of the terser breakage rather than anything about terser itself.\n\nRESOLUTION, per Peter\'s policy that this host uses pnpm and not npm:\n- npm uninstall -g terser  (removed; /usr/local/bin/terser npm copy gone)\n- pnpm setup               (created PNPM_HOME=/root/.local/share/pnpm, appended to /root/.bashrc)\n- pnpm add -g terser       (terser 5.50.0 at /root/.local/share/pnpm/terser)\n- /usr/local/bin/terser is now a WRAPPER script that execs the pnpm shim.\n\nWhy a wrapper and not a symlink: pnpm\'s shim computes its package dir from dirname($0). Symlinked into /usr/local/bin it looks for /usr/local/bin/global/5/node_modules/... and fails. exec\'ing the real path keeps $0 correct. Tried the symlink first and it failed exactly this way.\n\nWhy a wrapper is needed at all: PNPM_HOME is exported from ~/.bashrc, which non-interactive shells (PlatformIO build hooks) do not source, so terser would be invisible to the build otherwise.\n\nVerified after: JS 49801->34120 (31.5%), no warning, http:// intact in the generated header, git shows no diff on include/dashboard_html.h.'}
2026-08-16 07:45:25,019 1202862 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_new args={'title': 'IMPLEMENT the true-state page - what is claimed, what is checked, and what nobody has looked at', 'description': 'Peter, 09:00: "I still have no clue what the true state of this project is" — asked of a board whose first requirement is that progress is visible. He had to ask a session, and the session answered with SQL. That is the product gap, with the query already written.\n\nThe page must lead with the UNCHECKED surface, not the checked one: specboard is 45 of 50 claims never verified and 0 proofs defined; device is 170 of 370 and 7 live contradictions. A page that showed only what passed would be a lie of omission.'}
