2026-08-16 08:49:45,231 1202862 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'goal', 'text': "Make a claim correctable, so the 420 claims — the surface that actually goes stale — can be fixed without a hand-written UPDATE against board.db.\n\nVerifying all 50 of specboard's claims produced four contradictions and three of them were wrong CLAIMS, not wrong code. The fastest route to fewer defects ran through a mechanism that did not exist.\n\nDone when: a correction needs a reason, keeps the pre-image, refuses identity fields by name, and — the part that is not like amending a defect — expires the verdicts that answered the old wording, because a claim's text is the thing that was verified."}
2026-08-16 08:49:51,648 1202862 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'plan', 'text': 'Generalise docs/modules/amending-a-defect.md, which was built to be generalised.\n\n1. claim_amendment table holding the PRE-image; claim updated in the same transaction so every reader stays current.\n2. /claims/amend refusing: no reason, empty text, and any field outside does/where/sym/section BY NAME.\n3. A verdict stamps the claim revision it answered; verify_state returns `stale` when the claim has moved since. Revision is DERIVED as a count over claim_amendment — no stored column to drift and no backfill.\n4. The correction form and the full prior-version history on the specs tab, behind a <details> so 370 claims are not buried under 370 forms.\n5. Assertions in check_drain, including the one that matters: a verdict recorded before the amendment reads stale after it.'}
2026-08-16 08:49:57,165 1202862 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_done args={'number': 1}
2026-08-16 08:49:59,682 1202862 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_done args={'number': 2}
2026-08-16 08:50:01,509 1202862 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_done args={'number': 3}
2026-08-16 08:50:03,610 1202862 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_done args={'number': 4}
2026-08-16 08:50:10,596 1202862 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_new args={'name': 'the-board-updates-itself', 'title': 'GAP - every figure needs a refresh to be believed, which is the standing requirement Peter has stated twice', 'steps': ['DOCUMENT the spec - a live feed on stdlib http.server, and why SSE rather than websockets', 'IMPLEMENT the event stream and the change signal', 'IMPLEMENT the client so every figure updates without a refresh', 'OBSERVE - two browsers, watch one change in the other, both themes']}
2026-08-16 08:50:13,028 1202862 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_complete args={'name': 'correct-a-claim'}
2026-08-16 08:50:55,217 1202862 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_file_attach args={'file_path': 'docs/modules/the-board-updates-itself.md', 'kind': 'plan', 'label': 'Spec - SSE not websockets, one version integer, and why'}
2026-08-16 08:51:00,948 1202862 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'goal', 'text': 'Satisfy the standing requirement Peter has stated twice: "everything that is not a Submission i.e form, should be a ws feed such that I can watch the dashboard change in front of me without refreshing the page."\n\nIt cost him on 2026-08-16: "i see no change on the board. still 17 defects" — said while looking at a page rendered before the change, with nothing telling him it was stale. A stale board is indistinguishable from a board reporting that nothing happened, which is the opposite of what this tool is for.\n\nDone when: a page left open notices a change made elsewhere and brings itself up to date, without the user refreshing, proven with two browsers.'}
2026-08-16 08:51:08,003 1202862 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'plan', 'text': 'DECISION TAKEN ALONE: Server-Sent Events, not websockets. Peter said "ws feed"; the requirement he stated is one-directional ("everything that is not a Submission"), this board is stdlib http.server with no dependencies, and a hand-rolled websocket handshake plus frame codec would be the largest machinery in the repo to carry traffic in a direction nothing sends. EventSource also reconnects by itself. Reversible: one route and one EventSource — the same version signal drives websockets if he wants them.\n\n1. A `version` integer bumped on every write that changes what a page would show.\n2. GET /live holds the connection open, Content-Type text/event-stream, sends the version immediately then on every change. Capped, because each listener holds a thread.\n3. Every rendered page carries the version it was rendered at; the client compares and reloads ITSELF when they differ. One integer, never a diff — sending changed values means a second renderer that can disagree with the first.\n4. tools/check_live.py: stream answers, version arrives unprompted, a write on another connection pushes a new one, reads do not bump it, the cap refuses gracefully.'}
