2026-08-16 09:24:05,029 1180635 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_new args={'name': 'ltc-est-life-net', 'title': 'EST LIFE is computed from gross current, so with a bias fitted and no DUT it reports a confident battery life for the bias resistor', 'steps': ['Investigate: trace estLifeH/fullLifeH callers, the dashboard render, and every consumer of est_h/full_h', 'Spec SPEC-ESTLIFE.md: which average the projection uses, what it shows below the trust floor, exact diffs', 'Implement exactly the spec', 'Observe: static grep, functional on-device with no load, regression on a loaded run', 'Track: hash, step done, commit']}
2026-08-16 09:24:19,080 1180635 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'goal', 'text': 'Peter started a run with NO load connected. The dashboard reports EST LIFE 80.7 d in large type, which reads as "a load is connected and here is how long it will last".\n\nObserved on device 2026-08-16 ~08:14 UTC, build 1751b2f-dirty, run_secs 509, nothing attached but the 1 kohm bias resistor:\n  est_h 1935.7 (= 80.7 d)   avg_ma 1.65 (GROSS)   dut_avg_ma -1.775 (NET)\n  bias_ma 3.4253  bias_r 1003.6  bias_ok true  vbat 2.87  below_floor TRUE\nDashboard math drawer states it outright: "est life 80.7 d = rem 3198.0 mAh / avg 1.65 mA".\n\nDefect: include/battery.h:317 estLifeH() and :324 fullLifeH() both use avgMa(), the GROSS average, which with a bias fitted is dominated by the bias resistor\'s own draw. The UI banner immediately above the card promises "headline figures are NET of this". The projection therefore contradicts the banner and answers a question nobody asked (how long the battery lasts discharging through the bias resistor).\n\nSecondary, same screen, same cause family:\n- MAH USED . NET reads 0.2 with no DUT attached.\n- below_floor is TRUE and the page correctly warns "apparent current below trust floor (2.3 mA) - sign and magnitude unreliable", yet EST LIFE is rendered confidently with only a +/-50% quantization caveat and is NOT marked unreliable, despite being derived from the same sub-floor pulses.\n\nSemantics to settle in Phase 2 (Peter\'s call): "life of this battery" (gross is arguably right) vs "life at the DUT\'s draw" (net). The bug is that the UI promises the second and computes the first. A projection built on a sub-floor, negative net current should render as "-" rather than a number.\n\nOVERLAP TO FLAG: task 462 ltc-est-sd already proposes changing est_h/full_h to fold in self-discharge. Same two functions. Coordinate or the two specs will conflict.'}
