2026-08-16 18:19:03,973 1202862 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'name': 'prove-specboard-against-itself', 'kind': 'goal', 'text': 'Make the dogfood test finite and then pass it. specboard\'s premise is two axes — matches and works — and it had verified 47 of its own 50 claims on the first and had ZERO proofs on the second, while demanding that axis of every repo it watches.\n\nPeter: "this is dogfood. until specboard proves itsels against itself, I can not contine with device." And immediately before: "my gut feeling is this is an infinite tunnel, I will never see any light."\n\nBoth answered by the same thing: a countable finish line. "No defects" is unreachable for a defect-finding tool pointed at itself, so while that is the exit the tunnel really is infinite.\n\nDONE WHEN: every claim either has a proof on the works axis or a written reason why no run can show it, and a real run is recorded. Reached — 30 of 51 proven, 21 explained, 11 of 11 proofs passing.'}
2026-08-16 18:19:17,354 1202862 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'name': 'prove-specboard-against-itself', 'kind': 'plan', 'text': "Verified step by step before closing, not from marks:\n\n1. spec — docs/modules/proving-specboard-against-itself.md exists\n2. proofs.define repaired — grep 'ON CONFLICT(project, name) DO UPDATE' proofs.py = 1\n3. check_states enters by the caller's door — 1 proofs.define(conn call\n4. proofs declared — 35 proof_of links for specboard\n5. runs recorded — 11 runs, 11 of 11 pass\n6. measured — declare_proofs --check: 30 of 51 proven, 21 unproven and every one explained\n\nShipped in 3100ee0 (the works axis) and d5c9014 (the run-wipe fix found while doing it)."}
