2026-08-16 20:18:54,838 1202862 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'goal', 'text': 'Make a closure say what proved it, so the weakest and strongest fixes stop looking identical on the board.\n\ndevice: "A SHA proves a commit EXISTS. It does not prove anything was run, reached, or observed." They closed two defects deliberately with evidence they called weak in their own report, and the board showed them exactly like a proof-backed closure.\n\nMy own spec (drawing-the-end-of-the-tunnel.md:80-82) had already specified both forms of evidence — a resolving commit OR a proof with a passing run. I built the first and documented the route as though it enforced both.\n\nDONE WHEN: `fixed` reads as `asserted` or `proven`, derived rather than stored, with a run that predates the fix counting for nothing; and every surface showing a closed defect shows which.'}
2026-08-16 20:19:12,810 1202862 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'plan', 'text': "Verified step by step before closing, not from marks. Shipped in be15586 (+ 781d6d9 for the stale allowlist entry it exposed).\n\n1. spec — docs/modules/a-fix-must-say-what-proved-it.md exists\n2. db.fix_evidence built — 1 definition; uses git merge-base --is-ancestor, memoised per (repo, fix, build)\n3. surfaces split — asserted_fixes/proven_fixes in db.py (4 refs) and render.py (3)\n4. device's two closures read `asserted, asserted` — exactly what they reported\n\ncheck_drain asserts all four cases including the one that matters: a proof that passed BEFORE the fix leaves it asserted.\n\nNOT DONE HERE, raised separately: verification/closing-a-defect-moves-no-axis — device's second finding, that closing a defect moves neither axis. That is the next task."}
