2026-08-16 20:28:12,751 1202862 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'goal', 'text': 'Enforce Peter\'s rule: "a new claim or fix cannot be started until a fix/step/claims that it was working on has been verified and works."\n\n"Verified and works" is the two axes by name. The board already knew whether a claim was verified against current code and had never used it to stop anything — which is why device could close two defects in radio-transport (55 claims, 0 verdicts) and move the proven surface by zero.\n\nDONE WHEN: starting new work is refused while claims citing the files of this party\'s own last fix are unverified; the refusal names them and the call that settles each; and the inbox and verification itself are never refused, because a gate that deadlocks gets removed.'}
2026-08-16 20:28:26,763 1202862 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'plan', 'text': 'Shipped 0ca038a. Spec: docs/modules/nothing-new-until-the-last-thing-works.md, hashes recorded.\n\n1. INVESTIGATE — four routes start work; only /defects/raise, /defects/rule and /inbox/hear carry `who`. /claims/raise does not, and correctly: `claim` has no author column. Nothing refused anything; the two matches for "unfinished" in app.py/db.py are comments (app.py:285, db.py:1806).\n2. DOCUMENT — the spec, including why refusing is right here when it was wrong for `fixed`: refusing a closure offers a lie that gets you through, refusing a start offers none.\n3. IMPLEMENT — db.owed_by() + Handler._gate() on /defects/raise and /claims/raise.\n4. Closing a defect now forces the claims it staled to be settled before the next start — which is the mechanism that makes closing move an axis.\n5. OBSERVE — PAC owes 40 on the live board, refused 409 naming each; verifying one dropped it to 39; reachability proven by removing the gate (303) and restoring it (409); inbox and api/verify both unrefused.\n\nSTILL OPEN: verification/closing-a-defect-moves-no-axis is only half addressed. The gate forces verification before the NEXT start; it does not prompt at the moment of closing. A party that closes and then stops is not caught.'}
